Origin: https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/5af9465ca890be679033d5fb0dc89b6ea071326b
Advisory: GHSA-fpwc-w8rq-cr92, CVE-2026-91766
Imported-by: deb.sury.org php7.4 7.4.33-31 0153 + 0161 (test SKIPIF), adapted to 7.3 (no HTTP_WRAPPER_KEEP_METHOD)

From: Alexandre Daubois <alex.daubois@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 09:12:03 +0200
Subject: Fix GHSA-fpwc-w8rq-cr92: strip credentials from user headers on
 cross-origin redirects

Authorization, Cookie and Proxy-Authorization set through the http context
were forwarded verbatim when follow_location sent the request to another
origin. They are now stripped from the user header bag whenever the
redirect target differs in scheme, host or port, including when the header
name is repeated or the bag uses malformed line endings.

Co-authored-by: Jakub Zelenka <bukka@php.net>
(cherry picked from commit 5af9465ca890be679033d5fb0dc89b6ea071326b)
(cherry picked from commit cc54cbc7d08d309dbeaba4e7c9243f9fefa2e333)
(cherry picked from commit eb3554af131ec1ff4874891e657b7dc9d91cfd7a)

Backport to PHP 7.3 of the deb.sury.org php7.4 patch:
- 7.3 has no HTTP_WRAPPER_KEEP_METHOD (php-src GH-11274, 8.1+, which Sury carries for 7.4 as 0152): the redirect flags
  are HTTP_WRAPPER_REDIRECTED plus the new HTTP_WRAPPER_STRIP_AUTH; POST headers are stripped on every redirect and
  307/308 redirects switch to GET without body, so the test expects a GET on the redirected hop
- the test of the php-src follow-up 106c5c3106 (ghsa-fpwc-w8rq-cr92-002.phpt, as ported to 7.2) is included
---
